# RevenueCat public SDK key (Android `goog_...` / iOS `appl_...`). Same key name for every workflow.
#
# Local dev / `npx expo run:android|ios`:
#   1) Copy this file to `.env` and paste your key from the RevenueCat dashboard, OR
#   2) Add `REVENUECAT_API_KEY` in Expo → Project → Environment variables → `development`, then run:
#        npm run env:pull:dev
#
# EAS Build (`eas build`): set `REVENUECAT_API_KEY` in Expo for each environment
# (`development` / `preview` / `production` — matches `eas.json`). Any EAS cloud build fails at
# config time if this is empty (see `app.config.ts`). Local Gradle release builds without `.env` can
# still ship a broken binary — use `eas build` or ensure `.env` is present when exporting.
# Use visibility “Sensitive” unless Expo docs require otherwise.
#
REVENUECAT_API_KEY=
